<title>POLAND: MONKIEWICZ GIVES UP GOVERNMENT JOB.</title>
<headline>MONKIEWICZ GIVES UP GOVERNMENT JOB.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>An influential cabinet economic adviser resigned from his post of the cabinet's undersecretary of state after Poland's biggest insurer PZU SA appointed him president, the government spokeswoman said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Professor Jan Monkiewicz handed over his resignation to Prime Minister Wlodzimierz Cimoszewicz,&quot; Aleksandra Jakubowska told a news briefing. </p>
<p>She added Cimoszewicz has not yet approved the resignation. Monkiewicz has been in charge of the government's privatisation policy, notably concerning financial institutions. </p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
